#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1149 expect=skipped domain=XX
#note "XX is a sponsor domain the IG does not define: its library rows (XX in FDA-SD1149-library.yaml) are the SDTM Model's and carry no core, so get_dataset_filtered_variables(key_name=core, key_value=Exp) can never match -> the rule is SKIPPED (CDW-F1, PLAN-unserved-key-name-skip), not a silent 0-finding pass. XXSEV is empty on every record, so a served key would have fired. Mechanism only: the map-backed provider; the production provider is proven in CustomDomainModelWalkStoreTest."
#library-include FDA-SD1149-library.yaml
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset XX label="Sponsor Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col XXSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col XXTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term"
col XXSEV   type=Char label="Severity/Intensity"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | XX | 01-701-1015 | 1 | HEADACHE |
CDISCPILOT01 | XX | 01-701-1023 | 1 | NAUSEA   |
